-- ccc4-s85-98-use-possession.l4 -- sections 85 to 98.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (PART III, Firearms and Other Weapons):
-- Use Offences (85 to 87), Possession Offences (88 to 98.1).  Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- How an offence section is encoded (fork F-OF, in NOTES.md):
--   * "Every person commits an offence who ..." is read as the definition of the offence: an unmet element answers JUST FALSE
--     (the section defines the offence by its elements, as a "means" does); a case outside a limb the text writes with "without lawful excuse"
--     ("without" limits the prohibition in its own wording) answers NOTHING; "do not apply to", "unless" and "No person is guilty" answer JUST FALSE.
--   * the class of thing an offence names is the `s 84(1) kind of thing` the person states (the most specific class that fits); a term of
--     section 2 is an input named `s 2 <term>: ...`; "possesses" (section 4) is a plain fact.
--   * the penalty subsection of each offence is three things: its class (indictable, summary, or both), its indictable limb (a Punishment) and
--     its summary limb, which states no penalty and so takes the answer of section 787(1) as an input (`s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence
--     punishable on summary conviction`, an input of type Punishment).
--   * Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.

§ `Use Offences`

§§ `Section 85(1) and (2) -- Using firearm, or imitation firearm, in commission of offence`
-- src:2008 | Use Offences
-- src:2009 | Using firearm in commission of offence
-- src:2010 | 85 (1) Every person commits an offence who uses a firearm, whether or not the person causes or means to cause bodily harm to any person as a result of using the firearm,
-- src:2011 | (a) while committing an indictable offence, other than an offence under section 220 (criminal negligence causing death), 236 (manslaughter), 239 (attempted murder), 244 (discharging firearm with intent), 244.2 (discharging firearm — recklessness), 272 (sexual assault with a weapon) or 273 (aggravated sexual assault), subsection 279(1) (kidnapping) or section 279.1 (hostage taking), 344 (robbery) or 346 (extortion);
-- src:2012 | (b) while attempting to commit an indictable offence; or
-- src:2013 | (c) during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence.
@ref s 85(1) (src:2008-2013)
GIVEN `the kind of thing used` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person uses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person uses it while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(1) the person commits an offence by using a firearm in the commission of an offence` MEANS
    IF     `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing used`
       AND `the person uses it`
       AND (`limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who uses a firearm" (an unmet element; and for paragraph (a): "other than an offence under section 220")
    WHERE
        -- (a) while committing an indictable offence, other than an offence under section 220, 236, 239, 244, 244.2, 272 or 273, subsection 279(1) or section 279.1, 344 or 346
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the person uses it while committing an indictable offence` AND NOT (`the offence is one that paragraph (a) excepts`)
        `the offence is one that paragraph (a) excepts` MEANS
               `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 220
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 236
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 239
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 244
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 244.2
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 272
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 273
            OR (`the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 279 AND `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 279.1
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 344
            OR `the indictable offence the person is committing, attempting to commit or fleeing after`'s `section` EQUALS 346
        -- (b) while attempting to commit an indictable offence
        `limb (b)` MEANS `the person uses it while attempting to commit an indictable offence`
        -- (c) during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence
        `limb (c)` MEANS `the person uses it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence`

-- src:2014 | Using imitation firearm in commission of offence
-- src:2015 | (2) Every person commits an offence who uses an imitation firearm
-- src:2016 | (a) while committing an indictable offence,
-- src:2017 | (b) while attempting to commit an indictable offence, or
-- src:2018 | (c) during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence,
-- src:2019 | whether or not the person causes or means to cause bodily harm to any person as a result of using the imitation firearm.
@ref s 85(2) (src:2014-2019)
GIVEN `s 84(1) imitation firearm: the thing used is an imitation firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it while committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(2) the person commits an offence by using an imitation firearm in the commission of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person uses it` AND (`the person uses it while committing an indictable offence` OR `the person uses it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` OR `the person uses it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence`) AND `s 84(1) imitation firearm: the thing used is an imitation firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person uses it` AND (`the person uses it while committing an indictable offence` OR `the person uses it while attempting to commit an indictable offence` OR `the person uses it during flight after committing or attempting to commit an indictable offence`) AND `s 84(1) imitation firearm: the thing used is an imitation firearm` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 84(1) imitation firearm is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who uses an imitation firearm" (an unmet element)

-- src:2020 | Punishment
-- src:2021 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 85(3) (src:2020-2021)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 85(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 85(3) (src:2020-2021)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 85(3) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
-- src:2022 | Sentences to be served consecutively
-- src:2023 | (4) A sentence imposed on a person for an offence under subsection (1) or (2) shall be served consecutively to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed on the person for an offence under subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 85(4) (src:2022-2023)
GIVEN `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other punishment is imposed for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other sentence is one to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85(4) the sentence must be served consecutively to the other punishment or sentence` MEANS
    IF     `the sentence is imposed for an offence under subsection 85(1) or (2)`
       AND (`the other punishment is imposed for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events` OR `the other sentence is one to which the person is subject at the time the sentence is imposed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any other punishment imposed on the person for an offence arising out of the same event or series of events and to any other sentence to which the person is subject at the time"

§§ `Section 86 -- Careless use of firearm, etc.; contravention of storage regulations, etc.`

-- src:2024 | Careless use of firearm, etc.
-- src:2025 | 86 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, uses, carries, handles, ships, transports or stores a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons.
-- src:2026 | Contravention of storage regulations, etc.
@ref s 86(1) (src:2024-2026)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person uses, carries, handles, ships, transports or stores it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does so in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(1) the person commits an offence of careless use of a firearm, etc.` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person uses, carries, handles, ships, transports or stores it` AND `the person does so in a careless manner or without reasonable precautions for the safety of other persons`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, uses, carries, handles, ships, transports or stores a firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`

-- src:2026 | Contravention of storage regulations, etc.
-- src:2027 | (2) Every person commits an offence who contravenes a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act respecting the storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising and mail-order sales of firearms and restricted weapons.
@ref s 86(2) (src:2026-2027)
GIVEN `the person contravenes a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the regulation respects the storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising or mail-order sales of firearms or restricted weapons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(2) the person commits an offence by contravening a storage regulation, etc.` MEANS
    IF     `the person contravenes a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act`
       AND `the regulation respects the storage, handling, transportation, shipping, display, advertising or mail-order sales of firearms or restricted weapons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who contravenes a regulation made under paragraph 117(h) of the Firearms Act respecting the storage" (an unmet element)

-- src:2028 | Punishment
-- src:2029 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:2030 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment
-- src:2031 | (i) in the case of a first offence, for a term not exceeding two years, and
-- src:2032 | (ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2033 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 86(3) (src:2028-2033)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 86(3) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 86(3)(a) (src:2028-2033)
GIVEN `it is a second or subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 86(3)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    IF `it is a second or subsequent offence`
    THEN Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- (a)(ii) in the case of a second or subsequent offence, for a term not exceeding five years
    ELSE Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`   -- (a)(i) in the case of a first offence, for a term not exceeding two years

@ref s 86(3)(b) (src:2033)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 86(3)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
§§ `Section 87 -- Pointing a firearm`

