GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person points it at another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1) the person commits the offence of pointing a firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing` AND `the person points it at another person`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, points a firearm at another person" (an unmet element; "whether the firearm is loaded or unloaded" makes no difference)
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

