§ `Possession Offences`

§§ `Section 88 -- Possession of weapon for dangerous purpose`

-- src:2041 | Possession Offences
-- src:2042 | Possession of weapon for dangerous purpose
-- src:2043 | 88 (1) Every person commits an offence who carries or possesses a weapon, an imitation of a weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition for a purpose dangerous to the public peace or for the purpose of committing an offence.
@ref s 88(1) (src:2041-2043)
GIVEN `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the thing is an imitation of a weapon` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person carries or possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is dangerous to the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the committing of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(1) the person commits an offence of possession of a weapon for a dangerous purpose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS NOTHING AND `the conduct` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the answer of s 2 weapon is not covered ("weapon" includes things not listed)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who carries or possesses a weapon" (an unmet element)
    WHERE
        -- a weapon, an imitation of a weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition
        `the thing named` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon`, (JUST `the thing is an imitation of a weapon`), (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing` OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`)))
        -- for a purpose dangerous to the public peace or for the purpose of committing an offence
        `the conduct` MEANS `the person carries or possesses it` AND (`the purpose is dangerous to the public peace` OR `the purpose is the committing of an offence`)

-- src:2044 | Punishment
-- src:2045 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2046 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:2047 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 88(2) (src:2044-2047)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 88(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 88(2)(a) (src:2044-2047)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 88(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 88(2)(b) (src:2047)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 88(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
§§ `Section 89 -- Carrying weapon while attending public meeting`

-- src:2048 | Carrying weapon while attending public meeting
-- src:2049 | 89 (1) Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, carries a weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition while the person is attending or is on the way to attend a public meeting.
@ref s 89(1) (src:2048-2049)
GIVEN `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person carries it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is attending or is on the way to attend a public meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89(1) the person commits an offence of carrying a weapon while attending a public meeting` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR NOT (`the person carries it` AND `the person is attending or is on the way to attend a public meeting`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who, without lawful excuse, carries a weapon" (an unmet element)
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the answer of s 2 weapon is not covered
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a weapon, a prohibited device or any ammunition or prohibited ammunition
        `the thing named` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon`, (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing` OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is ammunition or prohibited ammunition` `the kind of thing`)))

-- src:2050 | Punishment
-- src:2051 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 89(2) (src:2050-2051)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 89(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 89(2) (src:2050-2051)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 89(2) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
§§ `Section 90 -- Carrying concealed weapon`

-- src:2052 | Carrying concealed weapon
-- src:2053 | 90 (1) Every person commits an offence who carries a weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition concealed, unless the person is authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed.
@ref s 90(1) (src:2052-2053)
GIVEN `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person carries it concealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(1) the person commits an offence of carrying a concealed weapon` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the person is authorized under the Firearms Act to carry it concealed"
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR NOT `the person carries it concealed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who carries a weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition concealed" (an unmet element)
        IF `the thing named` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the answer of s 2 weapon is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing named` MEANS `s 84(1) some limb holds` (LIST `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon`, (JUST (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing` OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`)))

-- src:2054 | Punishment
-- src:2055 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2056 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2057 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
