        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person possesses it`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition" (an unmet element)
        IF `the person is the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without being the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it"
