§§ `Section 92 -- Possession of firearm, prohibited weapon, device or ammunition knowing its possession is unauthorized`

-- src:2075 | Possession of firearm knowing its possession is unauthorized
-- src:2076 | 92 (1) Subject to subsection (4), every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm knowing that the person is not the holder of
-- src:2077 | (a) a licence under which the person may possess it; and
-- src:2078 | (b) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it.
-- src:2079 | Possession of prohibited weapon, device or ammunition knowing its possession is unauthorized
@ref s 92(1) (src:2075-2079)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the person is not the holder of what the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 92(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(1) the person commits an offence of possession of a firearm knowing its possession is unauthorized` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 92(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to"
        IF NOT (`s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing possessed` AND `the person possesses it` AND (NOT (`the person holds what the subsection requires`)) AND `the person knows that the person is not the holder of what the subsection requires`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm knowing that the person is not the holder of" (an unmet element)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- knowing that the person is not the holder of (a) a licence under which the person may possess it; and (b) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it
        `the person holds what the subsection requires` MEANS
                `the person is the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it`
            AND (`the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` OR `the person is the holder of a registration certificate for it`)

-- src:2079 | Possession of prohibited weapon, device or ammunition knowing its possession is unauthorized
-- src:2080 | (2) Subject to subsection (4), every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition knowing that the person is not the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it.
@ref s 92(2) (src:2079-2080)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that the person is not the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 92(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92(2) the person commits an offence of possession of a prohibited weapon, device or ammunition knowing its possession is unauthorized` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 92(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to"
        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person possesses it` AND (NOT `the person is the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it`) AND `the person knows that the person is not the holder of a licence under which the person may possess it`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who possesses a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition knowing that the person is not the holder of a licence" (an unmet element)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`

-- src:2081 | Punishment
-- src:2082 | (3) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years.
