        -- (b) a person who comes into possession ... by the operation of law and who, within a reasonable period after acquiring possession of it, (i) lawfully disposes of it, or (ii) obtains a licence under which the person may possess it and, in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, a registration certificate for it
        `limb (b)` MEANS
                `the person comes into possession of it by the operation of law`
            AND (   `within a reasonable period after acquiring possession of it the person lawfully disposes of it`
                 OR (   `within a reasonable period after acquiring possession of it the person obtains a licence under which the person may possess it`
                    AND (   NOT (`the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm` OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`)
                         OR `within a reasonable period after acquiring possession of it the person obtains a registration certificate for it`)))

