§§ `Section 93 -- Possession at unauthorized place`

-- src:2090 | Possession at unauthorized place
-- src:2091 | 93 (1) Subject to subsection (3), every person commits an offence who, being the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or prohibited ammunition, possesses them at a place that is
-- src:2092 | (a) indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may not possess it;
-- src:2093 | (b) other than a place indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may possess it; or
-- src:2094 | (c) other than a place where it may be possessed under the Firearms Act.
@ref s 93(1) (src:2090-2094)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may not possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is other than a place indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is other than a place where it may be possessed under the Firearms Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(1) the person commits an offence of possession at an unauthorized place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 93(3) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possesses a replica firearm` `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possesses a replica firearm"
        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess it` AND `the person possesses it` AND (`the place is indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may not possess it` OR `the place is other than a place indicated on the authorization or licence as being a place where the person may possess it` OR `the place is other than a place where it may be possessed under the Firearms Act`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who, being the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess" (an unmet element)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing possessed`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing possessed`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`

-- src:2095 | Punishment
-- src:2096 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2097 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:2098 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 93(2) (src:2095-2098)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 93(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 93(2)(a) (src:2095-2098)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 93(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 93(2)(b) (src:2098)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 93(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
-- src:2099 | Exception
-- src:2100 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possesses a replica firearm.
@ref s 93(3) (src:2099-2100)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(3) subsection (1) does not apply to a person who possesses a replica firearm` MEANS
    IF `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a replica firearm`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a person who possesses a replica firearm" (it says nothing of a person who possesses something else)

§§ `Section 94 -- Unauthorized possession in motor vehicle`

-- Section 94(1) excepts an occupant who satisfies paragraph (a), for a firearm, or paragraph (b), for a weapon, device or ammunition.  The belief limbs
-- ("had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant ... could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament")
-- ask whether the occupant HAD reasonable grounds to believe it, not whether it is so: so the answer of the part that encodes sections 117.07 to 117.1 is not an element (Seams, NOTES.md).
-- src:2101 | Unauthorized possession in motor vehicle
-- src:2102 | 94 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), every person commits an offence who is an occupant of a motor vehicle in which the person knows there is a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition, unless
-- src:2103 | (a) in the case of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm,
-- src:2104 | (i) the person or any other occupant of the motor vehicle is the holder of
-- src:2105 | (A) a licence under which the person or other occupant may possess the firearm, and
-- src:2106 | (B) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, an authorization and a registration certificate for it,
-- src:2107 | (ii) the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant of the motor vehicle was the holder of
-- src:2108 | (A) a licence under which that other occupant may possess the firearm, and
-- src:2109 | (B) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, an authorization and a registration certificate for it, or
-- src:2110 | (iii) the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant of the motor vehicle was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament; and
@ref s 94(1)(a) (src:2101-2110)
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person or any other occupant is the holder of a licence under which the person or other occupant may possess the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or any other occupant is the holder of an authorization and a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of a licence under which that other occupant may possess the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of an authorization and a registration certificate for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(1)(a) the occupant is within the exception for a firearm` MEANS
    IF `limb (i)` OR `limb (ii)` OR `limb (iii)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless" paragraph (a) is met: when none of its limbs holds the exception is not met and the offence is not displaced
    WHERE
        `licence and, for a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, authorization and registration certificate: held` MEANS `the person or any other occupant is the holder of a licence under which the person or other occupant may possess the firearm` AND (`the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` OR `the person or any other occupant is the holder of an authorization and a registration certificate for it`)
        `licence and, for a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, authorization and registration certificate: believed` MEANS `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of a licence under which that other occupant may possess the firearm` AND (`the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a non-restricted firearm` OR `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of an authorization and a registration certificate for it`)
        -- (i) the person or any other occupant of the motor vehicle is the holder of (A) a licence ..., and (B) in the case of a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, an authorization and a registration certificate for it
        `limb (i)` MEANS `licence and, for a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, authorization and registration certificate: held`
        -- (ii) the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant of the motor vehicle was the holder of (A) ..., and (B) ...
        `limb (ii)` MEANS `licence and, for a prohibited firearm or a restricted firearm, authorization and registration certificate: believed`
        -- (iii) the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant of the motor vehicle was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament
        `limb (iii)` MEANS `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament`

-- src:2111 | (b) in the case of a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition,
-- src:2112 | (i) the person or any other occupant of the motor vehicle is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person or other occupant may transport the prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition, or
-- src:2113 | (ii) the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant of the motor vehicle was
-- src:2114 | (A) the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the other occupant may transport the prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device or prohibited ammunition, or
-- src:2115 | (B) a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament.
@ref s 94(1)(b) (src:2111-2115)
GIVEN `the person or any other occupant is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person or other occupant may transport it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of an authorization or a licence under which that other occupant may transport it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(1)(b) the occupant is within the exception for a weapon, device or ammunition` MEANS
    IF     `the person or any other occupant is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person or other occupant may transport it`
        OR `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was the holder of an authorization or a licence under which that other occupant may transport it`
        OR `the person had reasonable grounds to believe that any other occupant was a person who could not be convicted of an offence under this Act by reason of sections 117.07 to 117.1 or any other Act of Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless" paragraph (b) is met: when none of its limbs holds the exception is not met and the offence is not displaced

-- src:2120 | Exception
-- src:2121 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle who, on becoming aware of the presence of the firearm, weapon, device or ammunition in the motor vehicle, attempted to leave the motor vehicle, to the extent that it was feasible to do so, or actually left the motor vehicle.
@ref s 94(3) (src:2120-2121)
GIVEN `on becoming aware of the presence of it in the motor vehicle the person attempted to leave the motor vehicle, to the extent that it was feasible to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on becoming aware of the presence of it in the motor vehicle the person actually left the motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(3) subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant who attempted to leave or left the motor vehicle` MEANS
    IF     `on becoming aware of the presence of it in the motor vehicle the person attempted to leave the motor vehicle, to the extent that it was feasible to do so`
        OR `on becoming aware of the presence of it in the motor vehicle the person actually left the motor vehicle`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle who" attempted to leave or left (it says nothing of an occupant who did not)

-- src:2122 | Exception
-- src:2123 | (4) Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle when the occupant or any other occupant of the motor vehicle is a person who came into possession of the firearm, weapon, device or ammunition by the operation of law.
@ref s 94(4) (src:2122-2123)
GIVEN `the occupant or any other occupant is a person who came into possession of it by the operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(4) subsection (1) does not apply when an occupant came into possession by the operation of law` MEANS
    IF `the occupant or any other occupant is a person who came into possession of it by the operation of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle when the occupant or any other occupant ... is a person who came into possession" (it says nothing of other cases)

-- src:2101 | Unauthorized possession in motor vehicle
-- src:2102 | 94 (1) Subject to subsections (3) and (4), every person commits an offence who is an occupant of a motor vehicle in which the person knows there is a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition, unless
@ref s 94(1) (src:2101-2102)
GIVEN `s 2 motor vehicle: the vehicle is a motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is an occupant of the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of thing` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person knows there is such a thing in the vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 94(1)(a) the occupant is within the exception for a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 94(1)(b) the occupant is within the exception for a weapon, device or ammunition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 94(3) subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant who attempted to leave or left the motor vehicle` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 94(4) subsection (1) does not apply when an occupant came into possession by the operation of law` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94(1) the person commits an offence of unauthorized possession in a motor vehicle` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 94(3) subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant who attempted to leave or left the motor vehicle` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle who"
        IF `s 94(4) subsection (1) does not apply when an occupant came into possession by the operation of law` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to an occupant of a motor vehicle when"
        IF `s 2 motor vehicle: the vehicle is a motor vehicle` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR NOT (`the person is an occupant of the vehicle` AND `the person knows there is such a thing in the vehicle` AND `the thing is one that the subsection names`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who is an occupant of a motor vehicle in which the person knows there is a prohibited firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `the exception that applies to the thing` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless"
        IF `s 2 motor vehicle: the vehicle is a motor vehicle` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the answer of s 2 motor vehicle is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm, a non-restricted firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, other than a replica firearm, or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited device other than a replica firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`
        -- unless (a) in the case of a prohibited firearm, a restricted firearm or a non-restricted firearm, ...; and (b) in the case of a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition, ...
        `the exception that applies to the thing` MEANS
            IF `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing`
            THEN `s 94(1)(a) the occupant is within the exception for a firearm`
            ELSE `s 94(1)(b) the occupant is within the exception for a weapon, device or ammunition`

-- src:2116 | Punishment
-- src:2117 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2118 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding ten years; or
-- src:2119 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 94(2) (src:2116-2119)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 94(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 94(2)(a) (src:2116-2119)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 94(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 94(2)(b) (src:2119)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 94(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
-- src:2124 | (5) [Repealed, 2012, c. 6, s. 4]
@ref s 94(5), repealed (src:2124)
`s 94(5) as the text shows it` MEANS "(5) [Repealed, 2012, c. 6, s. 4]"

§§ `Section 95 -- Possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition`

-- src:2125 | Possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition
-- src:2126 | 95 (1) Subject to subsection (3), every person commits an offence who, in any place, possesses a loaded prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, or an unloaded prohibited firearm or restricted firearm together with readily accessible ammunition that is capable of being discharged in the firearm, without being the holder of
-- src:2127 | (a) an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess the firearm in that place; and
-- src:2128 | (b) the registration certificate for the firearm.
@ref s 95(1) (src:2125-2128)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person possesses it in a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is loaded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is unloaded and the person possesses readily accessible ammunition that is capable of being discharged in the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess the firearm in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the holder of the registration certificate for the firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 95(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(1) the person commits an offence of possession of a prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 95(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who is using the firearm under the direct and immediate supervision"
        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person possesses it in a place` AND (`it is loaded` OR `it is unloaded and the person possesses readily accessible ammunition that is capable of being discharged in the firearm`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who, in any place, possesses a loaded prohibited firearm or restricted firearm" (an unmet element)
        IF `the person is the holder of an authorization or a licence under which the person may possess the firearm in that place` AND `the person is the holder of the registration certificate for the firearm` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without being the holder of"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a loaded prohibited firearm or restricted firearm, or an unloaded prohibited firearm or restricted firearm together with readily accessible ammunition ...
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited firearm`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted firearm`

-- src:2129 | Punishment
-- src:2130 | (2) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1)
-- src:2131 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years; or
-- src:2132 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 95(2) (src:2129-2132)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 95(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 95(2)(a) (src:2129-2132)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 95(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

@ref s 95(2)(b) (src:2132)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 95(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`   -- the section states no penalty for this limb: the seam takes the answer of section 787(1), which another part encodes
-- src:2133 | Exception
-- src:2134 | (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who is using the firearm under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who is lawfully entitled to possess it and is using the firearm in a manner in which that other person may lawfully use it.
@ref s 95(3) (src:2133-2134)
GIVEN `the person is using the firearm under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who is lawfully entitled to possess it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is using the firearm in a manner in which that other person may lawfully use it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the person is using the firearm under the direct and immediate supervision of another person who is lawfully entitled to possess it`
       AND `the person is using the firearm in a manner in which that other person may lawfully use it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a person who is using the firearm under the direct and immediate supervision of another person" (it says nothing of anyone else)

§§ `Section 96 -- Possession of weapon obtained by commission of offence`

-- src:2135 | Possession of weapon obtained by commission of offence
-- src:2136 | 96 (1) Subject to subsection (3), every person commits an offence who possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition that the person knows was obtained by the commission in Canada of an offence or by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence.
@ref s 96(1) (src:2135-2136)
GIVEN `the kind of thing possessed` IS A `s 84(1) kind of thing`
      `the person possesses it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was obtained by the commission in Canada of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it was obtained by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 96(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) the person commits an offence of possession of a weapon obtained by the commission of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 96(3) subsection (1) does not apply to the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to a person who comes into possession"
        IF NOT (`the thing is one that the subsection names` AND `the person possesses it` AND (`the person knows that it was obtained by the commission in Canada of an offence` OR `the person knows that it was obtained by an act or omission anywhere that, if it had occurred in Canada, would have constituted an offence`)) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person commits an offence who possesses a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition that the person knows was obtained" (an unmet element)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        -- a firearm, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device or any prohibited ammunition
        `the thing is one that the subsection names` MEANS
               `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a firearm` `the kind of thing possessed`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a prohibited weapon`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: a restricted weapon`
               OR `s 84(1) the kind of thing is a prohibited device` `the kind of thing possessed`
               OR `the kind of thing possessed` EQUALS `s 84(1) kind: prohibited ammunition`

