§§ `Section 98 -- Breaking and entering to steal firearm`

-- src:2144 | Breaking and entering to steal firearm
-- src:2145 | 98 (1) Every person commits an offence who
-- src:2146 | (a) breaks and enters a place with intent to steal a firearm located in it;
-- src:2147 | (b) breaks and enters a place and steals a firearm located in it; or
-- src:2148 | (c) breaks out of a place after
-- src:2149 | (i) stealing a firearm located in it, or
-- src:2150 | (ii) entering the place with intent to steal a firearm located in it.
@ref s 98(1) (src:2144-2150)
GIVEN `the person breaks and enters a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person intends to steal a firearm located in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person steals a firearm located in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person breaks out of a place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had stolen a firearm located in the place before breaking out of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had entered the place with intent to steal a firearm located in it before breaking out of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) the person commits an offence of breaking and entering to steal a firearm` MEANS
    IF `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person commits an offence who" (an unmet element: none of paragraphs (a), (b) and (c))
    WHERE
        -- (a) breaks and enters a place with intent to steal a firearm located in it
        `limb (a)` MEANS `the person breaks and enters a place` AND `the person intends to steal a firearm located in it`
        -- (b) breaks and enters a place and steals a firearm located in it
        `limb (b)` MEANS `the person breaks and enters a place` AND `the person steals a firearm located in it`
        -- (c) breaks out of a place after (i) stealing a firearm located in it, or (ii) entering the place with intent to steal a firearm located in it
        `limb (c)` MEANS `the person breaks out of a place` AND (`the person had stolen a firearm located in the place before breaking out of it` OR `the person had entered the place with intent to steal a firearm located in it before breaking out of it`)

-- In this section, break has the same meaning as in section 321 (the answer of that part is an input), and place means ...
DECLARE `s 98(2) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 98(2) place: a building`
    `s 98(2) place: a structure`
    `s 98(2) place: part of a building or structure`
    `s 98(2) place: a motor vehicle`
    `s 98(2) place: a vessel`
    `s 98(2) place: an aircraft`
    `s 98(2) place: a railway vehicle`
    `s 98(2) place: a container`
    `s 98(2) place: a trailer`
    `s 98(2) place: a thing that is none of those`

-- src:2151 | Definitions of break and place
-- src:2152 | (2) In this section, break has the same meaning as in section 321, and place means any building or structure — or part of one — and any motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer.
@ref s 98(2) "place" (src:2151-2152)
GIVEN `the thing` IS A `s 98(2) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) place` MEANS
    IF `the thing` EQUALS `s 98(2) place: a thing that is none of those`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "place means any building or structure"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2151 | Definitions of break and place
-- src:2152 | (2) In this section, break has the same meaning as in section 321, and place means any building or structure — or part of one — and any motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft, railway vehicle, container or trailer.
@ref s 98(2) "break" (src:2151-2152)
GIVEN `s 321 the person breaks` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) break` MEANS `s 321 the person breaks`   -- "break has the same meaning as in section 321": the answer of the part that encodes section 321 is the answer here

-- src:2153 | Entrance
-- src:2154 | (3) For the purposes of this section,
-- src:2155 | (a) a person enters as soon as any part of his or her body or any part of an instrument that he or she uses is within any thing that is being entered; and
@ref s 98(3)(a) (src:2153-2155)
GIVEN `any part of the person’s body is within the thing that is being entered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any part of an instrument that the person uses is within the thing that is being entered` IS A BOOLEAN
