`s 98(3)(a) the person enters` MEANS
    IF     `any part of the person’s body is within the thing that is being entered`
        OR `any part of an instrument that the person uses is within the thing that is being entered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person enters as soon as any part of his or her body or any part of an instrument that he or she uses is within any thing that is being entered" (marginal reading: a "when" that fails)

-- src:2153 | Entrance
-- src:2154 | (3) For the purposes of this section,
@ref s 98(3) (src:2153-2154)
-- src:2156 | (b) a person is deemed to have broken and entered if he or she
-- src:2157 | (i) obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within, or
-- src:2158 | (ii) entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening.
@ref s 98(3)(b) (src:2156-2158)
GIVEN `the person obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(3)(b) the person is deemed to have broken and entered` MEANS
    IF     `the person obtained entrance by a threat or an artifice or by collusion with a person within`
        OR `the person entered without lawful justification or excuse by a permanent or temporary opening`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is deemed to have broken and entered if he or she" (marginal reading (a): a failed "if")

