      `the person commits it with intent to steal a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the course of the robbery the person steals a firearm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98.1 the person commits an offence of robbery to steal a firearm` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 343 the person commits a robbery within the meaning of section 343` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND (`the person commits it with intent to steal a firearm` OR `in the course of the robbery the person steals a firearm`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 343 the person commits a robbery within the meaning of section 343` EQUALS NOTHING AND (`the person commits it with intent to steal a firearm` OR `in the course of the robbery the person steals a firearm`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 343 is not covered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who commits a robbery within the meaning of section 343 with intent to steal a firearm or in the course of which he or she steals a firearm commits an indictable offence" (an unmet element)

